                        "name": "Vernon Mauery",
                        "email": "vernon.mauery@gmail.com",
                        "username": "vmauery"
                    },
                    "message": "If you define the response to the image as a bunch of boolean values, then you can just return responseSuccess(reserved6, scanningEnabled, eventsEnabled, senThreshold.lowerNonCritical, senThreshold.lowerNonCritical, senThreshold.lowerCritical, senThreshold.lowerCritical, ...);"
                },
                {
                    "file": "sensorhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 1534,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "I have a few questions:\n1. Why use bool as the return value? What are the advantages?\n2. If bool is used as the return value, there will be a lot of bool parameters, about dozens of them(IPMI Spec Table 35-11, Get Sensor Event Enable). Is it necessary to do this?\n\nIn addition, this method refers to the ipmiSenGetSensorEventEnable method in dbus-sdr/sensorcommands/."
                },
                {
                    "file": "sensorhandler.cpp",
                    "line": 1534,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "George Liu",
                        "email": "liuxiwei@ieisystem.com",
                        "username": "lxwinspur"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
